{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/916139-do-the-imbued-exist-in-the-current-world-of-darkness","id":916139,"title":"Do the Imbued exist in the current World of Darkness?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-17T05:35:13-07:00","id":916139,"title":"Do the Imbued exist in the current World of Darkness?","content":"My answer is no. The Imbued were created as a result of the metaplot event known as the Year of the Reckoning, which has not occurred in the twentieth-anniversary World of Darkness. Therefore, it seems logical that the Imbued do not exist in this world. Has anyone spotted any references to the Imbued in twentieth-anniversary products? Please let me know if you have, as it means I will need to revise my theory. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T06:32:09-07:00","id":916151,"title":"","content":"20th Anniversary products are deliberately metaplot agnostic - well, mostly - and don't exist to retcon everything after 1999. Events and splats from books after 1999 will exist, or not exist, as the ST desires. Further, as Imbued are explicitly referred to in Werewolf 20th, if one is insistent on viewing them as a distinct timeline rather than simply 'hey, here's a bunch of shit to bring an old product up to snuff', we can safely state that the Imbued exist in some form in the 20th Anniversary 'verse' as well as in the 'main' verse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T06:40:44-07:00","id":916155,"title":"","content":"Their existence or nonexistence is entirely up to you. There's no single correct canon for the &quot;current World of Darkness&quot; anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T06:55:39-07:00","id":916162,"title":"","content":"the whole &quot;The end is here!&quot; Theme has been dialed down in its urgency...<br /> <br /> if you want them to exist feel free though... to be fair though I usualy use hunters as whipping boys, or cannon fodder coopted by supernaturals.<br /> <br /> I really disliked the Imbued blanket immunity to supernatural coercien.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T07:16:28-07:00","id":916171,"title":"","content":"They only get that blanket immunity when their Hunter Sight is active, which they have to spend a point of Conviction to do. This might not seem like a big deal, but Conviction isn't super easy to replenish and hoarding it is also the only way to advance your powers. Coupled with the fact that they're otherwise still incredibly squishy and the situational immunity to mind powers becomes a lot less impressive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T07:19:38-07:00","id":916175,"title":"","content":"I've seen the Imbued referred to numerous times in 20th Anniversary books, so my answer is yes. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T07:35:35-07:00","id":916187,"title":"","content":"Repeat my answer from the same question regarding KotE? Until there's a book, the answers aren't really going to change.<br /> <br /> It seems a bit silly to go through this for everything that doesn't have a 20th book officially out or announced (regardless of if they ever do). The 20th books are not major retcons of the pre-existing game world, and are purposefully designed to be used at any state of the previously published metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T07:53:49-07:00","id":916198,"title":"","content":"Yeah a number of x20 books make reference to them. Of course since the Imbued are new and not organized, none of the supernaturals know much about them other than there are hunters out there now with powers that had never been seen before. Even V20 Hunters Hunted II points them out and that non-Imbued hunters are just as weary of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T08:11:25-07:00","id":916210,"title":"","content":"Thank you. I guess what I really wanted to know was whether the Imbued had been referenced in 20th anniversary products, and the answer appears to be a resounding yes. I am both surprised and pleased to hear this, as I always liked the Imbued. I don't own any 20th anniversary products except for Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra, at least partially because I always believed that they deliberately didn't include anything from Revised onward. Now that I know this is not the case, I may pick up a few. Thanks again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T08:41:38-07:00","id":918638,"title":"","content":"I dare to say maybe you could see future books about Imbueds in a new Dark Age: Inquisition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T11:59:07-07:00","id":918727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/916139-do-the-imbued-exist-in-the-current-world-of-darkness?p=918638#post918638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dare to say maybe you could see future books about Imbueds in a new Dark Age: Inquisition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except they are two very different kinds of Hunters and the Imbued did not exist until after the Sixth Great Maelstrom because they were created as a response to that event.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T09:21:05-07:00","id":920406,"title":"","content":"My opinion is we could forget somethings about cannon and metaplot because for 20th Ann maybe there is retcon. That means demons and imbuied in previous ages are possible. If the retcon is good for the background, then we can accept it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}